 "notes": {
  "mapping": "CNO-2001 codes assigned to personas by majority rule on INDEC's 2015 double-coded EPH (D-AR-09). Personas P02 (database and network), P04 (ICT managers), P05 (designers), P08 (data and research) and P09 (marketing) have no CNO-2001 code where they are the majority: their cells are empty, never zero. P01 then also holds most database and network professionals (91% of P01's 2015 employment was ISCO 251 or 252).",
  "size_bands": "PP04C bands cut at 10 and 200 people, as Colombia (Mexico cuts at 250).",
  "socioeconomic": "pct_ipcf_deciles_7_10 = household per-capita income deciles 7-10 of the total EPH (DECCFR), i.e. the two top quintiles; replaces Colombia's electricity stratum.",
  "geography": "EPH covers the 31 agglomerations only (about 63% of the population); provincial rows are the agglomerations of each province, not the whole province (D-AR-08)."
 },
 "limitations": "Urban sample survey; the panel rotates so one person can appear in up to 4 quarters (interviews counts records). Cells with fewer than 100 interviews are low confidence."
}